. Next.js Integration Strategy\\\\n   • Packages: firebase, firebase-admin, cookie, js-cookie, jsonwebtoken.\\\\n   • Client: firebaseClient.ts, AuthContext.tsx exposing {user, loading, role}.\\\\n   • HOC/Hook: withAuth(Component, requiredRole?), useAuth().\\\\n   • Server: firebaseAdmin.ts (singleton), middleware.ts verifies token cookie, sets x-user-role header, redirects unauth.\\\\n   • API helper getAuthUser(req) verifies cookie via admin SDK.\\\\n\\\\n6. Auth Token Flow\\\\n   After login: user.getIdToken() → httpOnly Secure cookie “token” (SameSite=Lax, 1h). Refresh listener renews. Logout clears.\\\\n\\\\n7. Dev / CI / Deploy\\\\n   • .env.local & Vercel env vars for client + admin.\\\\n   • GitHub Actions inject secrets.\\\\n   • firebase emulators:run + Jest unit tests.\\\\n\\\\n8. Dependency Handoffs\\\\n   A) CMS team → board claim access, useAuth() hook.\\\\n   B) Front-End → withAuth HOC, AuthContext, file-upload helper paths.\\\\n\\\\n9. Validation & Testing\\\\n   • Unit tests on rules via @firebase/rules-unit-testing.\\\\n   • Cypress e2e: auth, cookie, redirects, board access.\\\\n   • Security scan (npm audit, Snyk).\\\\n\\\\n10. Roll-out / Migration\\\\n   1) Merge PR behind feature flag → staging QA.\\\\n   2) Promote to prod → seed superadmin.\\\\n   3) Onboard board users via setUserRole.\\\\n\\\\nSUBORDINATE ROLES REQUESTED\\\\n  1. Supervisor – FirebasePlatformSupervisor (config, rules, CI)\\\\n  2. Supervisor – NextAuthIntegrationSupervisor (Next.js code, token cookies, middleware)\\\\n  3. Supervisor – RulesTestingSupervisor (unit & e2e tests, ≥95 % coverage)\\\\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"auth-plan-001\\\"\\n}\\n###rpt-auth-plan-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###auth-next-steps-001###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Delta (1)\\nTo: 3\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"[Orders from Delta (1) to Motti (3) with seque